## Parent

`PRD.md` (repo root). Section references below (e.g. §7.5) point at its numbered headings. This repo is greenfield: there are no existing source files, so file paths are defined by PRD §6 and by the earlier issues named under "Blocked by".

## What to build

Add the `opencode` provider by following the adapter pattern from the Claude adapter: spawn the `opencode` CLI headlessly with the worktree as cwd in its unattended/full-auto mode, stream output as events, report exit code, honor the abort signal, and fail fast at startup when the CLI is missing. Verified with a fake `opencode` executable on PATH; the real-login test is done by the user at the end. Covers PRD §6 and §9.

## Context: files to read before implementing

- `PRD.md` §6 (adapter mapping), §9 (existing CLI login, no stored credentials, not a sandbox).
- `src/providers/claude.ts`, `src/providers/claude.test.ts`, `src/providers/index.ts` from issue 04 — copy the structure.
- If `opencode --help` / `opencode exec --help` / `opencode run --help` is available locally, confirm the flag names; the intended mapping is: `opencode run <prompt>` with its permission prompts disabled/auto-approved, with `--model` passed through when given.

