The `opencode` provider is in place, and typecheck, lint and the full test suite pass (122 tests). All of it was tested against a fake `opencode`; the real logged-in run is still yours to do.

**What it runs:** I checked `opencode run --help` on your machine. The adapter calls `opencode run --auto --format json [--model …] [extra flags] -- <prompt>`, with the worktree as the working directory and stdin closed.
- `--auto` approves permission prompts automatically, except ones you've explicitly denied.
- Extra flags come from `GRAPH_EXECUTION_OPENCODE_ARGS`.
- The prompt is one argument after `--`, so it never goes through a shell and can't be read as a flag. I confirmed the real CLI accepts `--` by pointing it at a server address that doesn't exist, so the run did nothing.
- No credentials are read or stored.

**Output events:** I couldn't confirm the shape of `--format json` output without a real logged-in run. The adapter assumes the text events look like `{"type":"text","part":{"type":"text","text":…}}`, which is from memory. Any line that doesn't match, including stderr, is passed through as raw text, so nothing is lost if the format differs. But if it is different, the agent's messages will show up as raw JSON.

**Changes:**
- `src/providers/opencode.ts`: the adapter, built the same way as the claude and codex ones.
- `src/providers/index.ts`: registers `opencode` and fails at startup if the binary isn't on PATH.
- `src/providers/opencode.test.ts`: uses a fake `opencode` on PATH to check the arguments, working directory, events, a non-zero exit code, that aborting kills the process, the error when the binary is missing, and the startup check.
- `src/cli.test.ts`: two new tests. `--provider opencode` with no CLI exits 2 with a clear message, and the diamond graph runs end to end through the fake `opencode`.
- `src/providers/claude.test.ts`: the "not implemented yet" test used `opencode` as its example, so I changed it to an unknown provider name.

To check against the real CLI, run the diamond graph with `--provider opencode`. If the agent's messages appear as raw JSON lines, change `parseOpencodeLine` in `src/providers/opencode.ts` to match the actual format.
